    "situation": "The bank payment system has recovered. The main payment journey ran clean on two looks in a row, the last at 72 s.",
    "background": "Payments was deployed 56 s before the assessment, moving from release 1.3 to 1.5. At the same time the gateway stopped answering and the fraud screening primary began timing out.",
    "assessment": "There were three faults, and the incident commander took each action itself. The gateway process was down, so it restarted the gateway, which is now running; fraud screening calls to the primary were timing out at 1.0 s (p95 1811 ms against a 15 ms baseline), so it failed screening over to the standby, which now serves it. Payments release 1.5 still returned 503 on 42% of requests after that, so it rolled payments back from 1.5 to 1.3, and the main journey has run clean since.",
    "recommendation": "The ledger issue has been escalated (soon) to the operations team, who must find and correct the duplicate payment records, because the incident commander cannot change data. The data check showed 57 duplicates at assessment and 125 later, so operations should review the full count and its money effect. Keep payments on 1.3 and screening on the standby until release 1.5 and the screening primary have been investigated."
